<p>The headline result: SoftMoE* with budget ≤4 achieves 2.70 validation loss on C4 — better than any sparse MoE configuration, including the one with k=4 fixed experts — while using only 3.64 active experts on average in training (−9% compute) and 3.73 at inference. On HellaSwag OWT it reaches 48.48% vs. the Sparse MoE k=4 baseline of 47.23%, with ~10% fewer active experts.</p>
<p>Adding learned per-layer allocation (full SoftMoE with optimized η) typically improves downstream tasks further while concentrating compute in later layers. The trade-off: average active experts slightly increases as the model claims more budget for semantic-heavy final layers.</p>
