<!-- LISTEN FRIENDLY -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display:none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: SoftMoE — Soft Differentiable Routing for Mixture-of-Experts</h2>
    <p>Standard sparse Mixture-of-Experts models choose a fixed number of expert networks to activate per token per layer, hard-coded before training starts. This discrete top-k selection is non-differentiable, so gradients cannot flow through the expert-selection process. Every layer must use the same expert count regardless of whether it handles simple syntax or complex semantic reasoning.</p>
    <p>SoftMoE replaces the discrete top-k with a continuous LapSum relaxation. The LapSum function finds a differentiable threshold that assigns soft weights to all experts — weights that still sum to k, but can vary between 0 and 1 instead of snapping to binary. This makes the number of active experts per layer fully differentiable and therefore learnable.</p>
    <p>When trained on C4 with a global budget of 20 expert-activations across 10 layers, SoftMoE discovers that later layers benefit far more from additional experts than early ones. The top three of ten layers claim roughly 50 percent of the total expert budget, while early layers settle for one or two. This non-uniform pattern emerges from gradient descent, not from any human-specified prior.</p>
    <p>Experimentally, SoftMoE matches or outperforms standard sparse MoE on language modeling and downstream reasoning benchmarks while activating 10 to 27 percent fewer experts. On HellaSwag with OpenWebText, SoftMoE reaches 48.48 percent versus the sparse MoE baseline of 47.23 percent, using roughly 10 percent fewer active experts during inference.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：SoftMoE——专家混合模型的软可微分路由</h2>
    <p>标准稀疏专家混合（MoE）模型在训练开始前就固定了每个层、每个词元激活的专家数量k。这种离散的top-k选择是不可微的，梯度无法流经专家选择过程。因此，每层必须使用相同数量的专家，无论该层处理的是简单句法还是复杂语义推理。</p>
    <p>SoftMoE用连续的LapSum松弛替换了离散的top-k选择。LapSum函数求解一个可微分阈值，为所有专家分配软权重——这些权重之和仍等于k，但每个值可以在0到1之间连续变化，而非强制为二进制。这使每层激活的专家数量完全可微，因此可以通过梯度下降学习。</p>
    <p>在C4数据集上以10层全局预算K=20训练时，SoftMoE发现较深的层从额外专家中受益远多于浅层。前10层中的最后3层占据了约50%的专家预算，而浅层仅需1-2个专家。这种非均匀分配模式完全由梯度下降自动涌现，而非人为指定。</p>
    <p>实验表明，SoftMoE在语言建模和推理基准测试中匹配或超越标准稀疏MoE，同时减少10%至27%的激活专家数。在OpenWebText的HellaSwag任务上，SoftMoE以少约10%的推理专家激活数，实现48.48%的准确率，优于稀疏MoE基线的47.23%。</p>
  </div>
</div>

